---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PercentDemo from '../../components/showcase/PercentDemo.astro';
import { pathFor } from '../../lib/site';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---
<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Calculator % lab: dual-rule +/−× trial | rea.run"
  description="Self-hosted teaching demo for Windows Calculator–style percent: after + take percent of the first operand; after × divide by 100. Links to Microsoft open source and REA."
  path="/lab/calculator-percent/"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a class="quiet-link" href={pathFor(lang, '/lab/')}>← Lab</a>
      {' · '}
      <a class="quiet-link" href={pathFor('zh', '/lab/calculator-percent/')}>中文</a>
    </p>
    <p class="kicker mt-4">Lab · native contrast</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-3 text-4xl">Rebuild Calculator’s % button — try both rules</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4">
      Why does <strong>200 + 10%</strong> become <strong>220</strong>, while <strong>200 × 10%</strong> becomes
      <strong>20</strong>? The percent key is operator-dependent. Microsoft publishes Calculator sources, so you can
      arbitrate REA findings against named symbols. This page hosts a small dual-rule trial for operators — original
      rea.run prose, not a clone of the <a href="https://rea.tools/">rea.tools</a> homepage.
    </p>

    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-panel)] p-4">
        <dt class="kicker">With +</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Take 10% of the first number.<br />
          <code>10% of 200 = 20 → 200 + 20 = 220</code>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-panel)] p-4">
        <dt class="kicker">With ×</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Turn 10% into 0.1.<br />
          <code>200 × 0.1 = 20</code>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <PercentDemo lang="en" />

    <section class="prose-page mt-10">
      <h2>Readable rule (teaching summary)</h2>
      <pre><code>if (operation == multiply || operation == divide) &#123;
  percent = current / 100;
&#125; else &#123;
  percent = current * previous / 100;
&#125;</code></pre>
      <p>
        For <code>previous = 200</code>, <code>current = 10</code>: add path yields <strong>20</strong> then
        <strong>220</strong>; multiply path yields <strong>0.1</strong> then <strong>20</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Open-source arbitration</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value / link</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Public tree</td>
            <td><a href="https://github.com/microsoft/calculator">microsoft/calculator</a> (MIT)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Handler (pinned commit)</td>
            <td>
              <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/calculator/blob/d125246a4e19842ce1332e6c7839cf0e110027d8/src/CalcManager/CEngine/scifunc.cpp#L98-L111">scifunc.cpp · IDC_PERCENT</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Unit tests (pinned)</td>
            <td>
              <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/calculator/blob/d125246a4e19842ce1332e6c7839cf0e110027d8/src/CalculatorUnitTests/CalculatorManagerTest.cpp#L350-L370">CalculatorManagerTest.cpp</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Command IDs</td>
            <td><code>IDC_MUL 92 (0x5c)</code>, <code>IDC_DIV 91 (0x5b)</code>, <code>IDC_PERCENT 118 (0x76)</code>; constant <code>0x64 = 100</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <pre><code>case IDC_PERCENT:
&#123;
  // multiply/divide → X [op] (Y%)
  // otherwise → X [op] (X * Y%)
  if (m_nOpCode == IDC_MUL || m_nOpCode == IDC_DIV)
    result = rat / 100;
  else
    result = rat * (m_lastVal / 100);
  break;
&#125;</code></pre>

      <h2>Verifiable trial matrix</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Expected %</th><th>Expected result</th><th>Check on this page</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>200 + 10%</td><td>20</td><td>220</td><td>Select +, press %, press =</td></tr>
          <tr><td>200 × 10%</td><td>0.1</td><td>20</td><td>Select ×, press %, press =</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Operator steps</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Read the short showcase summary: <a href={pathFor(lang, '/showcase/windows-calculator-percent/')}>/showcase/windows-calculator-percent/</a>.</li>
        <li>Open the pinned <code>scifunc.cpp</code> and tests above; name the branch before trusting a screenshot.</li>
        <li>If you inspect an installed Calculator binary with REA, keep Evidence + public source side by side.</li>
        <li>Rebuild only teaching demos you control — not advice to tamper with OS components you are not authorized to modify.</li>
      </ol>
      <pre><code>Use REA to inspect Windows Calculator’s % button.
Recover the rules after + and ×, then build a small calculator that uses both.</code></pre>

      <h2>Teaching disclosures</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>This widget is an <strong>interactive illustration</strong> of the inspected percentage rule — not the Windows Calculator UI.</li>
        <li>Prefer Microsoft’s public MIT tree as the arbitration layer when claims conflict.</li>
        <li>Authorized / educational / interoperability study only. See <a href={pathFor(lang, '/compliance/')}>/compliance/</a> and <a href={pathFor(lang, '/faq/legal-boundary/')}>/faq/legal-boundary/</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Lab hub</td><td><a href={pathFor(lang, '/lab/')}>/lab/</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dino speed lab</td><td><a href={pathFor(lang, '/lab/dino-speed/')}>/lab/dino-speed/</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Showcase summary</td><td><a href={pathFor(lang, '/showcase/windows-calculator-percent/')}>/showcase/windows-calculator-percent/</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>DX-Ball Evidence</td><td><a href={pathFor(lang, '/showcase/dx-ball/')}>/showcase/dx-ball/</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Official REA</td><td><a href="https://rea.tools/">rea.tools</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Chinese twin</td><td><a href={pathFor('zh', '/lab/calculator-percent/')}>/zh/lab/calculator-percent/</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
